  {
    "type": "h1",
    "text": "Hi, I'm Jonathan Behrens",
    "links": [
      {
        "text": "",
        "href": "#h.8tl4re3ih4io"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "p",
    "text": "I am a mechanical engineering student at Messiah University (Class of 2027) and a space nerd. I have dreamt of pushing humanity to the stars since middle school, when I tried to build a converging-diverging nozzle for a model rocket out of aluminum foil. My interest and passion remain unchanged, but my skills (at least in material selection) have improved! That's what I hope you will find as you browse this collection of some of the work I have done. "
  },
  {
    "type": "p",
    "text": "A little more about me personally, I am a devout Christian, which means that I have a strong sense of ethics when it comes to the workplace, and a passion to share and explore our Creation. I love travelling internationally; thus far, I have visited Israel and the Palestinian Authority, Peru (where this picture was taken, in Taquile on Lake Titicaca), and just this summer, Greece and Türkiye. Part of the reason I love visiting other countries is learning languages; I am fluent in English and Spanish and am trying to pick up Greek and Hebrew. Throughout my grade school time, I was very active in Boy Scouts, where I held many leadership positions and led three model rocket design competitions. (Despite my competitive advantage, I don't think I ever won!) If you couldn't tell from the structure of this paragraph, I am not the most organized person, but I have never let that hold me back from doing work that I am passionate about, so without taking up more of your time, some of my work and project experiences are found following the links below:"
  },
